  "href": "/life/2026/02/14/prague",
  "title": "🇨🇿 Finally Found the Wishing Well in Prague! ⛲️",
  "date": "2026-02-13T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "🇨🇿 Finally Found the Wishing Well in Prague! ⛲️\n\nI hopped on a RegioJet bus from Munich to Prague, and honestly, I was impressed! 🚌 The bus felt brand new, complete with chargers and working Wi-Fi. 🔋💻\n\nwindow seat\n\n📶 The \"Lost Signal\" Struggle\n\nJust before crossing into Czechia, my signal vanished! 📵 I had to scramble to check if my data plan supported roaming. Pro-tip: I actually had to switch my network settings to T-Mobile / O2 to get back online. 📱🌐\n\n🚋 Vintage Vibes & Pop Culture\n\nPrague still runs those charming old tram models. 🚃 They felt so familiar! These PCC-style trams used to be popular all over the world, and seeing them here is like a blast from the past. 🏛️\n\ntram\n\nMost Chinese travelers know Prague from Jolin Tsai’s famous song Prague Square (布拉格广场). 🎤 I’ll admit, I was a little disappointed at first—the huge square in front of the museum is currently under metro construction. 🚧🏗️\n\nmetro construction\n\n🍺 Groceries & \"Herb Cola\"\n\nAlbert is the go-to local supermarket here. 🛒 Fun fact: beer is actually cheaper than water! 🍺💧 I also made sure to pick up some JoJo gummy candies. 🍬\n\n| beer | candy |\n|-|-|\n|beer | candy |\n\nI also stopped by Lidl, which used to be an old bank vault! 🏦 There’s a massive lock kept as a memorial. I tried Kofola, the local \"herb cola.\" It tastes a bit like Dr. Pepper... 🥤🌿\n\nvault\n\nBudget Tip: The exchange rate is roughly 25 CZK : 1 EUR (or 3:1 for RMB). Compared to the rest of Europe, Czechia feels much more affordable! 💰📉\n\n🎭 The Legend vs. Reality\n\nOld Town Square\n\nI walked from Wenceslas Square (Václvské náměstí) to the Old Town Square. Everyone gathers at the Prague Astronomical Clock (Pražský orloj) for the puppet show when the clock strikes the hour. 🕒🐥\n\nBut here’s the kicker: There is no wishing well in the square! 😮 I was told the song lyrics were just written to rhyme—there’s no well, and no \"white pigeons\" either! 🕊️❌\n\n🏰 Crossing the Vltava\n\nCharles Bridge\n\nI crossed the Charles Bridge (Karlův most), making sure to touch the sculptures for good luck. 🖐️✨ I moved from the Old Town into Malá Strana (Lesser Town). Honestly, the \"Lesser Town Square\" looks more like a parking lot than a square. 🅿️ And yep... still no wishing well. 🤷‍♂️\n\nLesser Town Square\n\n🗿 Art & Food\n\nFranz Kafka Sculpture: This giant mirrored head rotates every hour. It’s mesmerizing! 🤖👤\n\nThe Hanging Men\n\nThe Hanging Men: On the way to the Dancing House, I spotted two sculptures of men hanging over the street. 🕴️ It’s a powerful metaphor for an unstable life. 🏗️\n\nKynute: I found these! They are basically Czech mantou. 🥟 Way tastier than regular bread! 😋\n\n⛲️ The Discovery!\n\nAfter crossing Most Legií, I visited the Lennon Wall and tried to see the famous \"narrowest street\" (sadly, it was closed). 🎨🚧\n\nwishing well\n\nBut then... I found it! The Wishing Well at the Kafka Museum! ⛲️✨ No wonder the lyrics say, \"The view was too beautiful, I didn't dare to look.\" (那画面太美我不敢看). Success at last! 🎯\n\n🏰 Castle Views\n\nchanging of guard\n\nI started the climb up to Prague Castle. 🏰 Most of the main sights are free to walk through! Since the gardens are closed in February, there wasn't too much walking, but I caught the Changing of the Guard. 💂‍♂️⚔️\n\nThe panorama of the city from up there is incredible, though it is a bit tricky for selfies! 📸🏙️\n\npano\n\nI visited the Golden Lane—I'm not sure why they charge for it during the day, but it’s free after 16:00, so I waited and explored it then. 🏠🔑\n\ncastle\n\n🛤️ Final Thoughts\n\nstation\n\nPrague reminds me a lot of Qingdao. 🌊 The train station is a modest building because most of the infrastructure is hidden underground. 🚉 On my train out, they even offered free comic books to read! 📖🎈\n\ncomic",
